{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause (TEST bug), measured: the index render runs the store read path (first-read freshness fetch + one `git rev-parse` probe per read, `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:221`), about 6 git child processes for one audited ticket, 0.2-0.45 s unloaded. Deterministic repro: PATH shim git sleeping 0.8 s per call -> unchanged test fails with the same `TimeoutError` (1 failed, 68 s); 0 s -> passes.\nFix (tests/unit/test_audit_serve.py only): state-based readiness wait (started or thread exited), bind assertion on the listening socket, no client read deadline (hang -> suite pytest-timeout 300 s), companion occupied-port test.\nAfter: slow-git 0.8 s and 1.5 s shims -> passes (23 s / 41 s call). Mutants: readiness wait ignoring thread death -> companion hits the per-test timeout; binding 0.0.0.0 -> bind assertion fails. 11 audit modules 76 passed; make lint and make typecheck exit 0.\nDiscovered: synonymous-destined-cricket (probe-before-throttle git spawn). Gerrit change 3305."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793805588625119001,"uuid":"d595c8ab-3c4e-470c-83a1-3508ae92aace"}